## Photodegradation of Methylene Blue with Ti-MOFs
The evaluation of photocatalytic activities of the samples for the photocatalytic degradation of organic dyes was performed at ambient temperature $(25^{\circ}\mathrm{C})$ . The procedure was as follows: 15mg of sample was dispersed into $15~\mathsf{m L}$ of methylene blue (MB) aqueous solution $(500\quad\upmu\mathrm{mol}\quad\mathsf{L}^{-1})$ . The mixture was stirred continuously with a magnetic stirring bar for two hours in the dark to reach the adsorption equilibrium. The photocatalytic dye degradation was carried out by irradiating the suspension with a 300 W Xenon lamp. At different time intervals, analytical samples were withdrawn and analyzed by UV-Vis spectroscopy. The degradation efficiency was determined by dividing ${\mathsf C}/{\mathsf C}_{0}$ with time, where C is the remained MB concentration and ${\sf C}_{0}$ is the starting MB concentration.
